This is CX-P15's own read, NOT the independent reader required by CHARTER law 6. ROOT must send that reader before landing. Read current full statements and proofs. None of the 45 theorem conclusions contains an alternative-disjunct escape; conjunctions require all components. Implications, iff bridges, constructor laws and explicit computations are identified below rather than represented as discovery of new empirical guarantees. Pointed Refines requires an initial related pair, excluding an empty relation shortcut.

P5 (namespace Nanodregg.Lang.Contextual.P5):
- checkRefutation_sound: no disjunct; checker success supplies BOTH domain coverage and negative replay. Domain membership alone cannot give rejection. Empty domain is a legitimate finite empty question, not the only case.
- witnessed_sound: no disjunct; actual judge output yields BOTH membership and acceptance, not an assumed witness property. Out-of-domain probe exercises the membership conjunct.
- refuted_sound: no disjunct; actual judge output must reach accepted certificate, then universal domain exclusion. Retained-search failure alone is insufficient.
- no_certificate_never_refuted: no disjunct; algorithmic exclusion for arbitrary problem/list/limit, even when no completion exists. It does not assert satisfiability.
- exhausted_is_open: no disjunct; premise is failed retained search and conclusion is the specific open obligation. This is the deliberate status policy, not a global existence/impossibility result.
- refuted_ne_outside: no disjunct; constructor-distinction law, explicitly structural. No claim that syntax alone establishes an impossibility proof.
- not_unfilled_suspends: no disjunct; missing atom premise forces a suspended negation, not Boolean false/true. Mutation produces False.
- negation_preserves_suspension: no disjunct; premise says f is suspended, conclusion computes a DIFFERENT expression neg f with identical obligations. Evaluation law, not circular assertion about f.
- refines_refl: no disjunct; algebraic law with identity relation and actual input/output obligations. Reflexivity is intentionally true for every machine.
- refines_trans: no disjunct; two pointed simulations construct a third through intermediate successors. Premises do not simply contain the requested composite relation.
- simulation_receives: no disjunct; legal spec execution plus simulation constructs an implementation execution AND related endpoint. Empty trace is base case; arbitrary nonempty traces use input matching.
- narrowing_breaks_peer: no disjunct; actual legal spec input and missing implementation input contradict every pointed simulation, not merely one chosen relation.
- polarized_matching: no disjunct; BOTH polarity directions required. Transparent bridge from simulation fields to LANG-67 ours/theirs labels; mismatched constructors eliminate impossible ownership cases only.
- simulation_preserves_safety: no disjunct; spec safety and simulation establish impl safety through both peer and implementation outputs. Horizon zero is True by definition, but theorem covers every horizon and inductively checks successors. No deadlock-freedom/progress claim.
- price_refines: no disjunct; numeric cap growth and output inclusion construct the pointed stateful simulation. Vacuous output sets are allowed for safety; statement also covers nonempty sets and both states.
- price_seven_breaks: no disjunct; closed conjunction computes acceptance by cap ten and rejection by cap five. Both sides required, no assumed observation.
- price_seven_not_refinement: no disjunct; closed negative rules out ALL pointed relations using legal input seven.
- price_reply_expansion_not_refinement: no disjunct; closed negative rules out ALL pointed relations using new reply false at the pending state.
- four_status_session: no disjunct; closed computation of four requests, exact ordered statuses and evidence. Open then witness uses the same completion question with expanded retained search; refuted/outside are explicit subsequent questions.
- incomplete_certificate_refused: no disjunct; closed computation rejects inadequate coverage while retained search misses the positive candidate.
- positive_candidate_refutes_certificate: no disjunct; closed computation rejects full coverage whose claimed excluded candidate is accepted.
- out_of_domain_witness_refused: no disjunct; closed computation rejects an accepted but outside-domain retained candidate.
- uniform_coin_problem_refuted: no disjunct; closed finite-domain checker computation over two constant answers against both coin responses. Only this finite question is concluded; P1 supplies the separate all-substitution bridge.

P1 (namespace Nanodregg.Lang.Contextual.P1; eight Nullable names noted):
- eligible_iff: no disjunct; explicit Boolean/Prop representation bridge. Both express admissibility AND every interaction, intentionally a representation law.
- adding_obligation: no disjunct; exact equality-as-iff of old eligible family intersected with the new test. Neither old eligibility nor the new test alone proves the conjunction.
- required_implies_tested: no disjunct; inclusion plus universal required orthogonality restricts to tested interactions. Set antitonicity is the intended structural law; no converse asserted.
- eligible_antitone: no disjunct; same restriction preserves admissibility as well. Explicit lifting of the prior law, not a stronger empirical result.
- inspect_witnessed: no disjunct; computed witnessed result entails complete input identity, admission, and every actual returned test passing. No caller-supplied fabricated report premise.
- analyze_witnessed: no disjunct; computed search result entails domain membership, admission, and all interactions in its returned scope. All three required.
- analyze_refuted: no disjunct; computed checked refutation excludes any admissible passing member of the EXPLICIT domain. Does not quantify outside that domain.
- analyze_no_certificate: no disjunct; checked procedure never emits refuted without evidence, for any tests/domain/retained list. Does not assert a repair exists.
- gaveUp_never_verified: no disjunct; structural inspect branch cannot emit any witnessed a, regardless of admission/tests. It deliberately makes no theorem about arbitrary fabricated status data.
- daimon_distinction: no disjunct; conjunction explicitly pairs vacuous behavioral orthogonality of gaveUp with a NON-successful completion judgment. First conjunct is true by design; second records why it does not establish repair.
- singleton_judge: no disjunct; equality of complete old/new judge results for singleton original guard. A conservative representation bridge, including refusals; not a renamed claim of new capability.
- interaction_judge_verified_iff: no disjunct; expanded iff retains typing, all tests, all blocker/support conditions and budget. Existing judge law is applied to the actual interaction guard.
